<h1>Pronorm German Kitchens &mdash; Selling &amp; Ordering Guide</h1>
<p class="page-subtitle">The one-page orientation for selling Pronorm through Pinnacle Sales &mdash; the lines at a glance, how design and ordering work, and where every Pronorm resource lives.</p>

<h2>The line at a glance</h2>
<p>Pronorm is a premium fitted German kitchen brand, manufactured in Vlotho, Germany since 1945 and available in the US exclusively through Pinnacle Sales dealers. It fills the gap between entry-level German imports and ultra-premium brands like SieMatic and Poggenpohl — typical installations run $40,000&ndash;$150,000+.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Y-Line — the unique handleless kitchen.</strong> Integrated aluminum grip profile (stainless, bronze, or black anodized) built into the top of each front; rear handle rail can match or contrast. Pronorm's flagship.</li>
  <li><strong>X-Line — the classic handleless kitchen.</strong> Gently curved C-shaped handle profile in 10 color options for a seamless, unified look.</li>
  <li><strong>Proline128 — the ergonomic grid kitchen.</strong> 128mm planning grid; any cabinet height, floor-to-ceiling configurations; mixes freely with Y-Line and X-Line or push-to-open.</li>
  <li><strong>100+ door finishes</strong> — high-gloss and premium matt lacquer, anti-fingerprint organic glass, real wood veneers, laminates, ceramic and stone looks, textured melamines.</li>
  <li><strong>Built for American kitchens</strong> — 610mm (24&Prime;) base and tall cabinet depths standard, unlike most European brands at 560&ndash;580mm.</li>
</ul>

<h2>How selling Pronorm works</h2>
<ol class="step-list">
  <li><strong>Qualify the project.</strong> Pronorm wins design-forward, handleless, European-modern projects with real budgets. For contemporary projects below the Pronorm budget, <a href="/dealer-hub/product-deep-dives/eclipse">Eclipse</a> is the step-down answer inside your same portfolio.</li>
  <li><strong>Design &amp; specification.</strong> Pronorm design, catalogs, specification detail, and dealer resources live at <a href="https://pronormusa.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PronormUSA.com</a> — that's the system of record for the brand.</li>
  <li><strong>Ordering.</strong> All Pronorm ordering runs through the PronormUSA process — see the <a href="/dealer-hub/ordering">Ordering SOPs</a> page for where Pronorm fits alongside your WW Wood workflow.</li>
  <li><strong>Display &amp; showroom.</strong> Pronorm display standards and specifications are at <a href="https://pronormusa.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PronormUSA.com</a>; for merchandising help in your showroom, <a href="/dealer-hub/submit/?type=showroom-consult">schedule a consult</a>.</li>
  <li><strong>Support.</strong> For design, ordering, and service questions, start at <a href="https://pronormusa.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PronormUSA.com</a> or reach your Pinnacle territory rep — the <a href="/dealer-hub/support">Support &amp; Escalation map</a> has contacts.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Selling notes</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Lead with 610mm depth.</strong> Authentic German engineering that fits American kitchens — no compromise on counters, appliance integration, or storage. It's Pronorm's biggest edge over competing German brands in the US.</li>
  <li><strong>The three lines combine.</strong> Y-Line, X-Line, and Proline128 share one platform — mix handleless fronts with grid planning freely in one kitchen.</li>
  <li><strong>Sustainability story.</strong> Climate-neutral manufacturing since 2021, PEFC certified, "Furniture Made in Germany" mark — material for design-conscious clients.</li>
  <li><strong>Whole-portfolio play.</strong> A Pronorm showroom display anchors your contemporary story; Eclipse and Nevara cover the tiers below it so no modern project leaves your showroom.</li>
</ul>

